paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Proofpoint is known for advanced email security, threat protection, and robust DLP features, making it a popular choice for large enterprises and highly regulated industries. Its DLP engine offers deep content inspection and strong incident management workflows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Mimecast combines email security, archiving, continuity, and DLP in a single platform, making it well suited for organizations looking for an integrated email protection solution without managing multiple tools."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"Zscaler provides cloud-native DLP as part of its Zero Trust security platform, offering strong protection for cloud applications, remote users, and modern hybrid work environments. Its DLP extends beyond email to web and SaaS traffic."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"When evaluating email DLP solutions, consider factors such as deployment model (cloud, on-premises, or hybrid), compliance support, integration with Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace, detection accuracy, reporting capabilities, ease of management, and scalability. Pricing for these platforms is typically quote-based and varies by organization size and feature tier, so request demos and quotes from shortlisted vendors."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"t":"text","v":"The best solution depends on your organization's security requirements, existing infrastructure, regulatory obligations, and budget."}]}]}
